<title>GERMANY: Heating oil spill in the Rhine river.</title>
<headline>Heating oil spill in the Rhine river.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>German river police said on Friday about 26 tonnes of heating oil had spilled into the Rhine after a collision between two tankers on the river near the western city of Duesseldorf.</p>
<p>Environmental authorities in Duesseldorf said that the full extent of the damage would only become clear in the summer and that it was probably minimal.</p>
<p>River police said a German tanker collided with Dutch tanker late on Thursday. The German vessel was carrying a cargo of 930 tonnes of heating oil.</p>
</text>
